# ADOPTING AN EXISTING RESOURCE with an `import` block (Terraform >= 1.5).
# Scenario: someone created the GitHub OIDC provider by hand in the console.
#
# 1. Rename this file to import.tf and write the matching resource config (or let Terraform draft it):
#      terraform plan -generate-config-out=generated.tf
# 2. `terraform plan` shows "1 to import" - nothing is changed in the cloud yet.
# 3. Review the plan, then apply. The import block can be deleted afterwards.
#
# Why this beats `terraform import` on the CLI: it is code-reviewed, appears in plans, and is repeatable.
import {
  to = module.ci_cd.aws_iam_openid_connect_provider.github
  id = "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:oidc-provider/token.actions.githubusercontent.com"
}
